{
    "method": "logs.logsServicesCreate",
    "toolName": "logs-services-create",
    "operationId": "logs_services_create",
    "title": "List services with stats",
    "category": "Logs",
    "description": "Return the top-25 services by log volume in the window, each with log_count, error_count, and error_rate,\nplus a per-service sparkline. Use this as the entry point when triaging which services are worth alerting on\n— high volume × non-zero error_rate is the natural alert candidate. Far cheaper than walking\nattribute-values + per-service counts.\n\nPut all parameters in `query`:\n\n```json\n{ \"query\": { \"dateRange\": { \"date_from\": \"-24h\" } } }\n```",
    "requiredScopes": ["logs:read"],
    "annotations": {
